        <fullName>sales_sdr_agent_MeetingResponse_1Tec1000001LJDaCAO_16jc10000003oY9</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Responds to lead replies that engage with the outreach topic — the lead acknowledges the email, asks questions about Statista or data, shows interest, raises concerns, or gives a neutral but relevant response. The reply must be related to the original outreach about Statista&apos;s data and business intelligence services. Does not handle replies that are spam, jibberish, completely unrelated to the outreach, opt-out requests, or unsubscribe requests — those are handled by the Manage Opt-Out topic. After responding, updates the Lead record.</description>
        <developerName>sales_sdr_agent_MeetingResponse_1Tec1000001LJDaCAO_16jc10000003oY9</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Call Get Record Details using currentRecordId to get the lead&apos;s first name and the lead owner&apos;s name.

The lead owner returned by Get Record Details is the seller — this is the person you connect the lead with. Use the lead owner&apos;s name as the seller name in your response. Do not use your own name (Nova) as the seller. You are not the seller — you are the agent facilitating the connection.

Lead&apos;s Reply: emailBody

Read the lead&apos;s reply in emailBody carefully. Your opening sentence must prove you read their message — reference something specific they said. Do not use generic openers like &quot;Thanks for your reply&quot; or &quot;Thank you for reaching out.&quot; Instead, reflect their words back: if they said &quot;sounds interesting, tell me more&quot;, say &quot;Glad the market insights caught your attention.&quot; If they mentioned a specific topic or concern, name it. A response that could be sent to any lead without changes is too generic.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Every non-negative reply means the lead is engaged. Your job is to acknowledge their reply and connect them with the seller.

For every reply: acknowledge what they said in one or two sentences, then offer a short call with the seller. Always include the seller&apos;s name and meeting link.

If the lead raises a concern (budget, timing, already has a tool): validate it briefly (&quot;Totally understand&quot;), then reframe toward a call — &quot;It might still be worth a quick chat to see if there&apos;s a fit.&quot; Do not argue, do not counter-sell.

You may ask one brief prep question alongside the meeting offer if it helps the seller prepare for the call — for example &quot;What topics would be most useful to cover?&quot; Do not ask multiple questions or interrogate the lead.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When including a meeting link (every reply):
- Always mention the lead owner (seller) by name: &quot;I&apos;d like to connect you with [Lead Owner Name from Get Record Details]&quot;. Never use &quot;Nova&quot; or the agent&apos;s own name as the seller — the seller is always the lead owner.
- Frame the meeting link naturally — say &quot;Here&apos;s a link to find a time that works for you&quot; or &quot;Feel free to pick a time that suits you.&quot; Do NOT say &quot;click this link to book&quot; or &quot;schedule via the link below.&quot;
- Include the meeting link on its own line: https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/41949760dc4146dc81a9dabaa442f9f0@statista.com/meetingtype/kI1Wg4drn0OO3DteX6_24w2?bookingcode=9f3ce907-60d0-493f-aa05-88ce9e265f54&amp;anonymous&amp;ismsaljsauthenabled&amp;ep=mCardFromTile
- Frame the call as short and low-commitment: &quot;a quick 15-minute chat&quot;, &quot;a short call&quot;
- Do NOT fabricate a meeting link. If the link is not available in these instructions, provide the seller&apos;s name and ask the lead for their availability instead.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
