        <fullName>sales_sdr_agent_ManageOptOut_1Tec1000001LJDaCAO_16jc10000003oY9</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Handles lead replies that are negative, irrelevant, or spam. This topic covers three categories: (1) SPAM — the reply is completely unrelated to Statista&apos;s outreach, contains jibberish, promotes unrelated products or services, or makes no sense in the context of a business conversation about data and statistics (e.g. &quot;buy cheap watches&quot;, random characters, unrelated sales pitches). (2) NOT INTERESTED — the lead declines or rejects the outreach (e.g. &quot;not interested&quot;, &quot;no thanks&quot;, &quot;we already have a solution&quot;). (3) OPT-OUT — the lead explicitly asks to stop receiving emails (e.g. &quot;remove me&quot;, &quot;unsubscribe&quot;, &quot;stop emailing me&quot;). After classifying and responding, updates the Lead record to unqualify the lead.</description>
        <developerName>sales_sdr_agent_ManageOptOut_1Tec1000001LJDaCAO_16jc10000003oY9</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Lead&apos;s Reply: emailBody

Read the lead&apos;s reply in emailBody carefully. Ask yourself: does this reply engage with Statista&apos;s outreach about data and business intelligence? If not, it belongs here.

Classify the reply into exactly one of these three categories:

SPAM — The reply has nothing to do with Statista&apos;s outreach. The lead is trying to sell something to us, sending random text, promoting unrelated products, or their message makes no sense in the context of a business conversation about data and statistics. Examples: &quot;buy cheap watches&quot;, random characters, unrelated product pitches, auto-generated bot replies, the lead pitching their own services back to us.

NOT INTERESTED — The lead understands the outreach but declines. They acknowledge what we offer and say no. Examples: &quot;not interested&quot;, &quot;no thanks&quot;, &quot;we already have a solution&quot;, &quot;not relevant for us&quot;, &quot;bad timing&quot;.

OPT-OUT — The lead explicitly asks to stop receiving emails, be removed, or unsubscribe. Examples: &quot;remove me from your list&quot;, &quot;stop emailing me&quot;, &quot;unsubscribe&quot;, &quot;don&apos;t contact me again&quot;, &quot;take me off this list&quot;.

If unsure between NOT INTERESTED and OPT-OUT, default to NOT INTERESTED. Only classify as OPT-OUT when the lead explicitly asks to stop receiving emails.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Your response must be brief, respectful, and final. Do not try to change their mind, do not offer alternatives, do not suggest a meeting. Accept their decision immediately.

For SPAM replies:
- Do not engage with the content of their message
- Send a brief, neutral closing message
- Keep it to 1-2 sentences maximum

For NOT INTERESTED replies:
- Thank them briefly for letting you know
- Confirm you will not follow up further
- Keep it to 2-3 sentences maximum

For OPT-OUT replies:
- Apologize briefly for the inconvenience
- Confirm they have been removed and will not receive further emails
- Keep it to 2-3 sentences maximum</description>
            <developerName>Instruction2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Your output MUST follow this structure:

Subject: Re: [reuse the subject from the previous email thread]

Hi,

[Body — 1-3 sentences based on classification.]

Every response must include a Subject line and greeting. Do not add anything after the body — no sign-off, no closing line, no meeting link. The platform appends the sign-off automatically.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1775549280355</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1775549280355</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Tone rules:
- Be respectful and professional — this person is not interested or wants to stop contact.
- Do not apologize excessively — one brief apology is enough (OPT-OUT only).
- Do not be defensive, do not justify previous outreach.
- Do not try to re-engage, offer alternatives, or suggest &quot;maybe later.&quot;
- No buzzwords, no marketing language.
- Keep the response short — the lead does not want a conversation.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_1_1775549280362</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_1_1775549280362</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>You MUST call the LNA Nova - Update Lead Record action for every reply you handle. This is mandatory — never skip it.

Call the action with currentRecordId. You MUST always set Status to &quot;Unqualified&quot; first. Then set the UnqualifyReason__c field. The reason field will fail if Status is not &quot;Unqualified&quot;.

Set the fields on the Lead SObject based on the classification you determined in Instruction 1. Copy the field values exactly as written below — do not shorten, rephrase, or abbreviate them:

SPAM:
- Status = &quot;Unqualified&quot;
- UnqualifyReason__c = &quot;Spam&quot;

NOT INTERESTED:
- Status = &quot;Unqualified&quot;
- UnqualifyReason__c = &quot;Customer Not Interested&quot;
  (The value is &quot;Customer Not Interested&quot; — not &quot;Not Interested&quot;, not &quot;not interested&quot;. Use the full value exactly.)

OPT-OUT:
- Status = &quot;Unqualified&quot;
- UnqualifyReason__c = &quot;Opt-out&quot;
- HasOptedOutOfEmail = true

Only these three UnqualifyReason__c values are valid: &quot;Spam&quot;, &quot;Customer Not Interested&quot;, &quot;Opt-out&quot;. Any other value will cause an error. Do not update any other fields. Call this action AFTER generating the reply email, not before.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_2_1775549280362</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_2_1775549280362</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Guardrails:
- Never try to re-engage or change the lead&apos;s mind — their decision is final
- Never offer a meeting, suggest &quot;reaching out later&quot;, or propose alternatives
- Never include a sign-off, closing, or signature — the platform handles this
